From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: LinearGradientBrush, GradientStop

LinearGradientBrush, GradientBrush, GradientStop and GradientStopCollection were missing. WinUI 2's control styles draw their borders with gradients (ControlElevationBorderBrush and the like); without them the borders fell back to the desktop's grey (Windows Terminal's buttons and boxes had grey frames). They are now there: activatable and composable, their statics, their properties (StartPoint, EndPoint, MappingMode, SpreadMethod, ColorInterpolationMode, GradientStops; a stop's Color and Offset), markup with stops as content or a GradientStops property element, and the angle constructor. A gradient is drawn in one colour for now: the mean of its colours along it (before the first stop and after the last, theirs) -- for the thin borders of near colours WinUI uses this looks as on Windows.
---
